  "description": "Reclaimed fodder grass packed for kulon and other livestock. A mature plant yields thirty-six units of fodder for six-tenths of a water ration. It grows more slowly than pundi rice but stretches irrigation water further when feeding a herd. Harvest and store it before allowing animals into the beds: grazing wastes much of the crop. It cannot replace edible grain in cooking or fuel processing.",
